1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,360
The tudor revival beanie institute building was designed by architect a h campbell.
这座都铎复兴风格的 Beanie Institute 建筑由建筑师 A. H. Campbell 设计；名称依字幕待核。

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:16,000
And opened on the 11 th of september 1899 to house the canterbury museum and public library that had originated on guildhall street.
作者说，它在1899年9月11日开放，用来容纳原在 Guildhall Street 的坎特伯雷博物馆和公共图书馆。

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,394
Free to enter it also holds the tourist information office an art gallery and free to use toilets.
免费进入，里面也有游客信息处、美术馆和免费厕所。

4
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:41,892
On the corner of best lane and the high street is a statue of geoffrey chaucer dressed as a pilgrim.
Best Lane 与 High Street 的拐角有一座杰弗里·乔叟的雕像，装束像朝圣者。

5
00:00:41,892 --> 00:00:46,480
He was the famous middle ages poet and author of the canterbury tales.
他是著名的中世纪诗人，也是《坎特伯雷故事集》的作者。

6
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:50,240
The 30 characters from the book are depicted on the plinth below him.
书中的三十个人物被刻画在他脚下的基座上。

7
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:59,298
Almost opposite the statue is eastbridge hospital not a hospital as we use that word today.
雕像几乎正对面是 Eastbridge Hospital；并不是今天通常所说的医院。

8
00:00:59,298 --> 00:01:04,000
But a place of hospitality for weary pilgrims travelling to canterbury cathedral.
它是为前往坎特伯雷大教堂的疲惫朝圣者提供接待的地方。

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,280
Open since the 12 th century for the last 400 years it's been an almshouse and still houses some elderly people.
作者说它从十二世纪起开放，近四百年来作济贫院，今天仍有一些老人住在里面。

10
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:30,805
One of the most photographed buildings in canterbury the old weaver's house is a lovely half timbered building on the river stour.
坎特伯雷最常被拍照的建筑之一，老织工之家，是斯陶尔河边漂亮的半木构建筑。

11
00:01:30,805 --> 00:01:34,611
The river runs right past the building and under the high street.
河水紧挨着建筑流过，再从商业大街下方穿过。

12
00:01:34,611 --> 00:01:41,526
The house takes its name from the influx of flemish weavers who settled in the area having fled religious persecution.
房子因涌入当地的佛兰芒织工而得名；他们逃离宗教迫害后在此定居。

13
00:01:41,526 --> 00:01:46,053
Elizabeth I granted them the right to establish their businesses in canterbury.
作者说伊丽莎白一世准许他们在坎特伯雷建立自己的生意。

14
00:01:46,053 --> 00:01:55,280
Believed to date back to the 14 th century even though the sign says 1500 most of the current building is from a reconstruction in the 16 th century.
虽牌子写1500年，据说可追溯至十四世纪，但现存建筑大部分来自十六世纪的重建。

15
00:01:56,320 --> 00:02:02,936
At the rear of the house is a medieval ducking stall jutting out over the river you can just see it there in the distance.
屋后有一座中世纪的 ducking stall，伸到河面上；远处刚好能看见。

16
00:02:02,936 --> 00:02:08,890
This ducking stool was historically used as a method of punishing people and it may well have included witches.
作者说，这种浸水椅过去用于惩罚人，受罚者可能也包括被指为女巫的人。

17
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:16,909
Dunked under the water and held for several minutes if she didn't drown she was proved a witch if she drowned well never mind her name was cleared.
作者讲述她们被浸入水中数分钟，不淹死就被当作女巫，淹死便算洗清名声；这是其讲述的历史说法。

18
00:02:16,909 --> 00:02:25,000
Canterbury's historic river tour company offers regular punts along the river leaving from the back of the weaver's house.
作者介绍，当地历史河游公司定期提供平底撑船游，从织工之家后面出发。

19
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:34,720
Moving to a side street we walk the friars passing the pilgrim hotel and a collection of period properties that are opposite the marlowe theatre.
转到一条侧街，我们沿 The Friars 走，经过 Pilgrim Hotel 和一排位于马洛剧院对面的老式房屋。

20
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:47,860
Named after christopher marlowe a famous elizabethan playwright born in canterbury and who attended king's school here in the city.
剧院以克里斯托弗·马洛命名，他是著名的伊丽莎白时代剧作家，生于坎特伯雷，曾就读本市 King's School。

21
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:53,360
The canterbury tales pub is just named such and has nothing to do with the author or the tales.
Canterbury Tales 酒吧只是用了这个名字，与作者或故事本身无关。

22
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:58,400
This brings us back to a river crossing catching glimpses of the cathedral.
这里让我们回到一处过河点，途中不时瞥见大教堂。

23
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:10,686
This delightful area is home to a sculpture by rick kirby called the bulkhead although his own website names it mask.
这片宜人的地方有 Rick Kirby 的雕塑，名为 Bulkhead，不过作者说艺术家自己的网站称它为 Mask。

24
00:03:10,686 --> 00:03:16,302
Behind it is the 1315 beerlings hall previously a guest house for pilgrims.
后面是1315年的 Beerlings Hall，以前是供朝圣者住的客舍；专名依字幕待核。

25
00:03:16,302 --> 00:03:28,143
Take a moment on the bridge to enjoy the scenery maybe see some of the visitors experiencing a punt on the river stour hearing tales of the past from their guide.
在桥上停一会儿欣赏风景，也许能看见游客在斯陶尔河上乘撑船，听导游讲过去的故事。
